WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.600
The narration is a synthetic voice.

2
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.293
This guide shows how to use Pravrudhi-Nyaya on a matter.

3
00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:08.250
This is a screening aid, not legal advice. A lawyer decides.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.415
On Matter tools you add the papers of a matter.

5
00:00:12.415 --> 00:00:15.420
The papers you add here are kept as text in our store,

6
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.871
in the EU (Romania), until you delete the paper or the matter.

7
00:00:18.871 --> 00:00:22.265
Keep the matter number: it is lost when you reload this page,

8
00:00:22.265 --> 00:00:27.162
and your matters cannot be listed here. Deleting removes them from this service's store.

9
00:00:27.162 --> 00:00:28.275
Images are not read.

10
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.943
The tools below use those papers, except the Section

11
00:00:34.943 --> 00:00:39.017
138 checklist, which counts from dates you confirm. Papers for a matter.

12
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:42.752
Add the papers of a matter and find a passage in them. Chronology.

13
00:00:42.752 --> 00:00:47.449
Lists the dates it reads in your papers, each with its sentence. May be incomplete.

14
00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:52.825
Review agenda. Lists the ingredients of the cheque-dishonour offence and the papers to look in.

15
00:00:52.825 --> 00:00:57.975
Citation sweep. Checks that each citation in your papers exists in our index, nothing more.

16
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.491
Quashing agenda.

17
00:01:00.491 --> 00:01:05.444
Lists the Supreme Court's quashing categories; does not say whether any applies.

18
00:01:05.444 --> 00:01:11.326
Cheque case check. Shows the review agenda and candidate dates per step; you confirm each date.

19
00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:17.022
Hearing pack. Gathers the dates, papers still to add and citations to look up for a hearing.

20
00:01:17.022 --> 00:01:18.384
Section 138 checklist.

21
00:01:18.384 --> 00:01:23.275
Counts section 138 periods from dates you confirm: a checklist, not a decision.

22
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.413
Papers you add to a matter.

23
00:01:26.413 --> 00:01:32.090
What is sent: each paper you add on Matter tools is sent to our service. Only its text is kept.

24
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:37.169
Where it is kept: in our store on a storage volume in the EU (Romania), not in India.

25
00:01:37.169 --> 00:01:40.216
How long: until you delete the paper or the matter.

26
00:01:40.216 --> 00:01:44.100
Nothing expires it, and we make no promise of a retention period.

27
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.489
What delete does: deleting a paper or a matter removes it,

28
00:01:53.489 --> 00:01:56.155
and its stored text, from this service's store.

29
00:01:56.155 --> 00:02:00.125
We have not tested what the underlying hosting storage may still hold.

30
00:02:00.125 --> 00:02:03.698
Who can read it: only your organisation, through the product or

31
00:02:03.698 --> 00:02:07.498
your organisation's API key; another organisation gets "not found".

32
00:02:07.498 --> 00:02:10.164
This service does not encrypt the stored files.

33
00:02:10.164 --> 00:02:13.850
People who run the service and its hosting account can read them.

34
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.270
Backup: none known.

35
00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:21.942
This service makes no copy, and we have not tested what our hosting provider keeps.

36
00:02:21.942 --> 00:02:27.065
The matter number is lost when you reload the page, and your matters cannot be listed here.

37
00:02:27.065 --> 00:02:32.300
If you lose the matter number, there is not yet a tested way to ask us to delete your papers.

38
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.895
To try the tools without your own papers, load a sample matter.

39
00:02:40.895 --> 00:02:45.315
The sample matter is invented: an invented FIR, chargesheet extract,

40
00:02:45.315 --> 00:02:48.500
bail order and cheque memo, with no real parties.

41
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.718
Each tool has a line saying what it does. This is a screening aid, not legal advice.

42
00:02:55.718 --> 00:02:56.875
A lawyer decides.

43
00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:57.800
The narration is a synthetic voice.
